---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Crumbs from '../components/Crumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
import { crumbLd, webPageLd } from '../lib/ld';

const crumbs = [{ name: 'How we verify', path: '/how-we-verify/' }];
const desc = 'How WeldFacts checks welder specs: manufacturer pages and manuals only, a citation on every row, and no estimated amps or thickness.';
const jsonld = [webPageLd('How we verify welder specs', '/how-we-verify/', desc, SITE.checked), crumbLd(crumbs)];
---
<Base title="How we verify welder specs" description={desc} path="/how-we-verify/" og="/og/page-how-we-verify.png" jsonld={jsonld}>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <div class="pagehead">
      <Crumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
      <h1>How specs are checked</h1>
    </div>
    <p>A number is a fact only when the manufacturer page or that maker's manual states it. The row links the URL. 2 November 2026 is the read date.</p>
    <h2>Sources</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The maker's product page, including a spec list on that page.</li>
      <li>The spec-sheet PDF linked from that page. Miller and Hobart sheets are on the ITW content host.</li>
      <li>The owner's manual PDF from the maker. Harbor Freight manuals are on manuals.harborfreight.com. Rebel EMP 215ic figures are from ESAB manual 0463 789 001.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Retail pages, forums, and other roundups are not sources. When one brochure disagrees with itself, both sentences stay. Rebel EMP 235ic says 53 lb in the intro and 63 lb in the spec table. The weight sort uses 63 lb. The cell shows both.</p>
    <h2>Missing fields</h2>
    <p>The cell says "Not published by manufacturer." Tip catalogs are not a wire range unless the sheet says the machine is set up for those wires. An example about a 10 minute cycle is not a new duty rating. E7018 is not turned into the word steel.</p>
    <h2>Outlet and thickness</h2>
    <p>208-240 V, 230 V, and 240 V match the 240 V chip. 110 V, 115 V, and 120 V match the 120 V chip. 460 V and 575 V match neither.</p>
    <p>Input current at rated output is not a breaker size. Above the breaker you set: fail. Fits, and the sheet names no breaker: warning. A pass needs a printed breaker size. Handler 210i has 15 A and 20 A rows. The 215ic manual also prints a 30 A time-delay max and a 50 A normal-fuse max.</p>
    <p>Single pass with no second maximum: a thicker job warns. A printed maximum that is not called single pass: a thicker job fails. Gauge is not converted to inches.</p>
    <p>The 10 minute bar reads the first percent already printed for that voltage. It does not pick a second duty point and it does not invent one.</p>
    <p>Aluminum on TIG passes only when the page names aluminum. DC TIG that never names aluminum fails that metal. Any other unnamed metal is left unscored.</p>
    <h2>Two files</h2>
    <p>Harbor Freight has two manuals for Unlimited 200, item 57862. Input current does not match. This site cites 57862-193175459367.pdf only.</p>
    <h2>Prices</h2>
    <p>No prices. Amazon links are searches. Tag weldfacts-20. No ASIN is verified in this version.</p>
    <p><a href="/contact/">Corrections</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
